   "description": "The bottom of the roasting pan is a bed of onion, leek, garlic, carrots, and celery. The turkey sits on top of it. Save the vegetables and drippings, they are the base for the gravy (separate page)."
  },
  {
   "name": "Butter Mixture",
   "lines": [],
   "description": "1.5 to 2 sticks of softened UNSALTED butter. Add lots of pepper and 3/4 of a pack of fresh thyme and mix well. It should be well speckled. Spread onto the entire turkey. Under the skin on the breasts will yield the best result."
  },
  {
   "name": "In the Cavity",
   "lines": [],
   "description": "Slice the lemon in half and push one half in first. Cut large chunks off a quartered onion. Do not chop fine, you want big pieces, and insert as much as you can. Add the remaining sprigs of thyme and close up the end with the other half of the lemon."
  }
 ],
